#: ../pwntools/docs/source/util/crc.rst:7
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.util.crc` --- Calculating CRC-sums"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:1
msgid "Module for calculating CRC-sums."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:3
msgid ""
"Contains all crc implementations know on the interwebz. For most "
"implementations it contains only the core crc algorithm and not e.g. "
"padding schemes."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:6
msgid ""
"It is horribly slow, as implements a naive algorithm working direclty on "
"bit polynomials. This class is exposed as `BitPolynom`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:9
msgid ""
"The current algorithm is super-linear and takes about 4 seconds to "
"calculate the crc32-sum of ``'A'*40000``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:12
msgid "An obvious optimization would be to actually generate some lookup-tables."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc:14
msgid "This doctest is to ensure that the known data are accurate:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc.BitPolynom:1
msgid "Class for representing GF(2)[X], i.e. the field of polynomials over GF(2)."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc.BitPolynom:4
msgid ""
"In practice the polynomials are represented as numbers such that `x**n` "
"corresponds to `1 << n`. In this representation calculations are easy: "
"Just do everything as normal, but forget about everything the carries."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.crc.BitPolynom:8
msgid "Addition becomes xor and multiplication becomes carry-less multiplication."
msgstr ""

