"\"printf\" builtin (e.g. Android 5.0 emulator images)."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:216
msgid "Toybox Shell"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:218
msgid "Android 6.0 (and possibly other versions) use a shell based on ``toybox``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:220
msgid ""
"While it does not include a ``printf`` builtin, ``toybox`` itself "
"includes a POSIX-compliant ``printf`` binary."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:223
msgid "The Ash shells should be feature-compatible with ``dash``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:226
msgid "BusyBox Shell"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string:228
msgid ""
"`BusyBox's Wikipedia page`_ claims to use an ``ash``-compliant shell, and"
" should therefore be compatible with ``dash``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_command_with:1
msgid ""
"Returns a command create by evaluating `f(new_arg0, ..., new_argN)` "
"whenever `f` is a function and `f % (new_arg0, ..., new_argN)` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_command_with:4
msgid ""
"If the arguments are purely alphanumeric, then they are simply passed to "
"function. If they are simple to escape, they will be escaped and passed "
"to the function."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_command_with:8
msgid ""
"If the arguments contain trailing newlines, then it is hard to use them "
"directly because of a limitation in the posix shell. In this case the "
"output from `f` is prepended with a bit of code to create the variables."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:1
msgid ""
"Outputs a posix compliant shell command that will put the data specified "
"by the dictionary into the environment."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:4
msgid ""
"It is assumed that the keys in the dictionary are valid variable names "
"that does not need any escaping."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:7
msgid "The variables to set."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:9
msgid "Should the variables be exported or only stored in the shell environment?"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:11
msgid "A valid posix shell command that will set the given variables."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_prepare:14
msgid "It is assumed that `var` is a valid name for a variable in the shell."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_string:1
msgid "Outputs a string in a format that will be understood by /bin/sh."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_string:3
msgid ""
"If the string does not contain any bad characters, it will simply be "
"returned, possibly with quotes. If it contains bad characters, it will be"
" escaped in a way which is compatible with most known systems."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.util.sh_string.sh_string:9
msgid ""
"This does not play along well with the shell's built-in \"echo\". It "
"works exactly as expected to set environment variables and arguments, "
"**unless** it's the shell-builtin echo."
msgstr ""

